# Provider preparation helper: review required before execution

Created `prepare-provider-development.py` in this SDD directory only. SHA256 `d843fc553621565add6bc017a5f07975e98e48b8164e96b45e7c631039f8679f`. Scoped Ruff reports `All checks passed!`; built-in compile on source bytes passes without imports. The helper was NOT run. No core, config, campaign, image, credentials or runtime artifacts were changed.

## Intended invocation and input

After controller review, source application, the new image and all four authentic refreshed parent panels: run Python with `-B` against the absolute helper path, `--input-file ABSOLUTE_JSON`, cwd the final applied source checkout, in the same elevated environment as the eventual campaign launch. Do not run the preparation in default mode then launch elevated: PATH/PATHEXT differences have already caused authenticated host identity mismatch. The helper imports only the final checkout at execution, never staging.

The input JSON must explicitly supply these fields:

- source_root: final checkout absolute path; source_commit: authenticated policy commit; target_pct: selected existing target string; campaign_id: new unique final campaign name; artifact_root: new nonexistent absolute repository root.
- proposal_path and proposal_sha256: exact reviewed `development/provider-campaign-proposal-20260907.json`. Its model/caps are consumed rather than copied from memory. The current recommendation is openai/gpt-5.4, six calls, 448000 total tokens, 8192 output tokens per role, overhead4096, audit-only USD with null price authority, zero retries/repair; two rounds/one hypothesis/one variant; role300/quick600/discovery1200/round7200/campaign14400 seconds. These remain a proposal, not remote-call approval.
- sandbox_profile_path: the new sealed canonical SandboxProfileV5 JSON; expected_runtime_source_sha256: the explicitly selected new runtime (controller currently building 005064e57e80840f3b2a97d7db694b176832b8f982996e63efc8a35064505ed4); baseline_plan_path: refreshed plan with profile_sha256, image_reference and window_selection.windows, matching the existing runtime parent planner shape.
- parent_run_directories: four absolute completed run directories in ordinal order. Each requires verification-record.json, cleanup-record.json, request/panel-request.json, output/panel-evaluation.json, in the same shape as the actual prior preparation helper.
- quick_panel_ref: explicit relative_path and sha256. assets: exactly three objects with source (absolute), target (canonical repository-relative), sha256: the exact PIT bundle, provenance and selected quick panel. Targets are data/pit_bundle.sqlite3, data/prices_provenance.json and quick_panel_ref.relative_path. No old manifests/profiles/baselines/journals are copied.
- operator_paths: exactly source_root, workspace_root, data_root, output_root, control_root, git_executable, docker_executable. Workspace/output/control must be fresh nonexistent paths; source/data and executables must already be real inputs accepted by normal preparation. No response_directory. Paths should use short controlled roots as prior Windows runtime work established.

## Actual API flow and authority

The helper validates proposal/profile/plan identities and actual four-panel verification/cleanup receipts, then lets prepare_development_campaign_v5 validate the full real requests/outputs and source/data/plan contract again. It never rebinds an old output to a new profile. It uses the normal importer for a clearly labeled provider-free `preparation-seed` manifest because that API exposes only four evaluator/round timeouts. Existing build_campaign_manifest_v5 then builds a distinct final manifest with the same authenticated dependencies and dataclasses.replace(resources, role_call_timeout_seconds=300). The controller explicitly accepted this existing-API approach. No source workaround or invented baseline report is used.

Only the final manifest is passed to prepare_development_adapter_config_v5, which creates the actual config and owner and derives paid gateway/ledger host identities without a completion or credential read. The normal command renderer emits the exact resume-campaign command in campaign-launch-input.json; no launch/round start is persisted. The seed has no config, owner, packet or invocation.

For the initial packet, the helper uses LocalArchiveReducerFactoryV5's initial projection, select_parent_v5 and LocalRoleRequestFactoryV5.investigator_request—the actual initial runtime path. It checks that no checkpoint exists. It exports initial-role-request.json, initial-response-schema.json, and initial-outbound-body.json, with request/schema/body hashes and prospective_role_usage_v5 bounds in review-disclosure.json. This is an actual prospective packet from authentic fresh baseline authority, not a synthetic role output or executed test. No invoker, reserve/complete method, round driver or evaluator is called.

The body is the exact logical outbound messages/schema/model/options using the existing wire serializer and current transport arguments. It is canonical review encoding, not a claim that SDK JSON whitespace or request header bytes are pre-rendered. The disclosure covers X-Session-Id campaign/hash metadata, deadline-bound timeout, zero SDK retries and OpenRouter compatible-upstream routing (no pinned upstream/fallback promise). Authorization header values are neither read nor exported.

Author and critic packets cannot be rendered exactly before actual preceding responses/evaluation. The disclosure specifies their existing typed source/aggregate envelopes and per-call durable request/budget binding. Author may receive all four editable policy files for cross-policy work even though full-source escape is false; this is explicitly disclosed. Later packets remain subject to existing cumulative token/call caps; a six-call completion is not guaranteed. USD upper bound remains null, with audited provider usage, not an invented price guarantee.

## Review and operational limits

This is create-only preparation, not a transaction: if validation fails after the new root or seed is written, preserve that evidence and use a new named preparation root after diagnosing it. Never rerun into the same root or treat the error as permission to delete state. New workspace/output/control directories likewise require deliberate cleanup after partial preparation. Static checks do not prove runtime preparation; the controller must review before actual execution.

Manual future Luna handoff should give exact source/helper hashes, fresh profile/baseline plan refs, this input shape, final manifest/config/owner and exact command. Explicitly explain the seed/final distinction, role-timeout API gap, same-elevation identity requirement, long Windows paths, no-tests/no-probes restriction, no inherited journal, and pending external authorization. Do not start a new Luna session automatically. No remote call may occur until model/destination/routing/caps/source-and-evidence disclosure are explicitly approved.
